om observations by the 20-record cutoff, proposals with a hypothesis, a minimum sample and risks, and a \"What not to change\" section.\n\n**On substance:**\n- Giving TEP-0006, 0009 and 0010 split verdicts is backed by the data.\n- The R2 gate rejections, which the reviewer flag hides, are counted separately and the data-quality issue is noted.\n- The limits (planner estimates, `out_of_context_reads`, same model family) are stated openly, not glossed over.\n\n**Weak points, none serious enough to reject:**\n- **TEP-0011 bundles five changes** under one hypothesis, so AUD-6 won't be able to tell which one worked. Splitting it, or measuring each part on its own, would be better.\n- **TEP-0012's 75% approval guard** for the new types is equal to this period's overall rate, so it adds little protection.\n- **The O1 record lists can be misread.** PKT-0087 appears in both causes, and PKT-0093 was fixed by hand, so the \"7 records\" figure is easy to misread.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Audit is complete, matches the scoreboard data, and gives sound, measurable proposals; the follow-up choice is justified in the log.","ttft_ms":2485,"type":"result","duration_ms":20687,"uuid":"3f954a97-d54d-4b13-b0fb-f1c6635f46e9","ttft_stream_ms":1101,"time_to_request_ms":492,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":366,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":21,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":7,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":22,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":5,"request_build":11},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":29,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":177,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":208,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":137,"process_rs